      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good base, but it feels a little bit thin for a full study guide. Could you expand on it a bit? \n\nMaybe add some more detail about the specific stages (prophase, metaphase, etc.) and why each part matters. Also, since our ranking tool is looking for those pedagogical markers I mentioned earlier, try to make sure the tone feels really instructional. \n\nJust a reminder again: don't let the score dictate the quality. I'd rather have a slightly lower score with great info than a high score with a bunch of filler. But definitely try to make it more comprehensive.",
